# EVONIX WiFi fragment (optional, dispatch only)
# Applied on top of evonix.config when the workflow runs with use_wifi=true.
# Brings the 802.11 stack (absent from the GKI base) plus the RTL8821AU
# out-of-tree USB driver ((CONFIG_RTL8821AU) for monitor mode + frame
# injection on adapters like TP-Link 2357:011f.
#
# Symbol notes:
# - CONFIG_WLAN=y: in-tree menu (drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig, bool,
#   default y) — entry requirement for the Realtek vendor block.
# - CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_REALTEK=y: in-tree Kconfig bool, default y.
# - CONFIG_CFG80211/CONFIG_MAC80211=y: wireless stack the driver speaks
#   through (CONFIG_IOCTL_CFG80211 path). MAC80211 select-lines pull
#   CRYPTO/CRC32 automatically; GKI already carries CCM/CMAC/AES.
# - CONFIG_RFKILL=y (not =m): tristate with no depends. Forced to y because
#   a =m RFKILL silently drags CFG80211/MAC80211/RTL8821AU down to =m via
#   Kconfig tristate logic, and =m needs modules.bzl registration + a
#   dist/copy step this workflow lacks. Keep RFKILL_INPUT off (INPUT stays
#   at its in-tree default; the driver does not need RF switch input).
# - CONFIG_RTL8821AU=y: out-of-tree driver Kconfig (tristate, depends on
#   USB — GKI carries USB host). Builtin only, same =y rule as CIFS.
CONFIG_WLAN=y
CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_REALTEK=y
CONFIG_CFG80211=y
CONFIG_MAC80211=y
CONFIG_RFKILL=y
CONFIG_RTL8821AU=y
